WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.111 --> 00:00:18.973
Anna cried as everyone else gasped.

2
00:00:19.913 --> 00:00:22.335
"Why do you think Anna stole the tickets, Henry?"

3
00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.496
Nathan asked.

4
00:00:23.516 --> 00:00:28.660
"She's the only one with the motive and the opportunity," Henry said.

5
00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:33.251
"She's been saving to buy a game player, so we know she needed money.

6
00:00:34.252 --> 00:00:39.096
When she got to that tide pool first, she decided to go grab the booty for herself."

7
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.878
William turned to Anna.

8
00:00:41.898 --> 00:00:43.479
"Is that true?"

9
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.761
Anna's shoulders slumped.

10
00:00:45.781 --> 00:00:47.963
"I didn't mean to do it!

11
00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:49.104
It was an accident."

12
00:00:50.085 --> 00:00:51.045
Maggie scowled.

13
00:00:51.066 --> 00:00:53.928
"How can you steal something by accident?"

14
00:00:53.948 --> 00:00:56.550
"Yeah!" chimed in Luke.

15
00:00:57.931 --> 00:00:58.652
Anna sighed.

16
00:00:59.796 --> 00:01:04.139
"I was about to check one tide pool when I realized that another one is shaped like a

17
00:01:04.179 --> 00:01:06.581
teardrop. Just like the clue!"

18
00:01:06.961 --> 00:01:07.662
Anna went on.

19
00:01:07.682 --> 00:01:10.684
"So I got excited and ran to that one."

20
00:01:10.704 --> 00:01:16.568
"That must be when Roger saw you running on the beach," Cole said.

21
00:01:16.588 --> 00:01:21.571
"When I got to the tide pool, nobody else was there yet," Anna went on.

22
00:01:21.592 --> 00:01:24.734
"I spotted the box in the water and grabbed it.

23
00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.676
I thought the envelope had money inside."

24
00:01:28.692 --> 00:01:30.192
"So you decided to steal it?"

25
00:01:30.413 --> 00:01:31.233
Maggie demanded.

26
00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:34.974
"I was thinking about taking some of it," Anna admitted.

27
00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.454
"Enough to buy myself a game player.

28
00:01:38.395 --> 00:01:40.615
I had gum in my pocket," she went on.

29
00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:43.256
"So I dropped that in the box.

30
00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:46.597
I thought the gum might make up for taking some of the money."

31
00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:48.718
Tears filled her eyes.

32
00:01:48.738 --> 00:01:52.299
"I know it was wrong—really wrong."

33
00:01:53.319 --> 00:01:54.959
Luke was staring at her in disbelief.

34
00:01:54.979 --> 00:01:57.500
"I can't believe you stole our stuff!"

35
00:01:58.864 --> 00:01:59.704
Anna bit her lip.

36
00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:04.806
"Once I realized that the envelope didn't have money, I wanted to put it back in the box.

37
00:02:05.826 --> 00:02:07.127
But I heard someone coming.

38
00:02:07.987 --> 00:02:10.208
I panicked and stuck the envelope in my pocket.

39
00:02:11.008 --> 00:02:14.629
Then I tossed the box back in the water and sneaked away before anyone saw me."

40
00:02:15.809 --> 00:02:16.970
Nathan frowned at Anna.

41
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.690
"How could you do something like that?"

42
00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.831
"I'm sorry."

43
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:24.312
Tears rolled down Anna's cheeks.

44
00:02:26.216 --> 00:02:28.837
She pulled an envelope out of her pocket and gave it to Henry.

45
00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:31.578
"I never meant to ruin anyone's fun.

46
00:02:32.639 --> 00:02:36.020
I just wasn't thinking, and now I feel terrible.

47
00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.841
I don't even want a video game player anymore!"

48
00:02:40.182 --> 00:02:42.603
Henry couldn't help feeling a little sorry for Anna.

49
00:02:42.623 --> 00:02:46.325
"I made a terrible mistake," she went on.

50
00:02:46.345 --> 00:02:48.426
"And I owe your parents a big apology too, William."

51
00:02:48.446 --> 00:02:48.906
He nodded coolly.

52
00:02:48.926 --> 00:02:49.566
"You sure do, Anna."

53
00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:51.707
Looking miserable, Anna headed back to the beach house to apologize to William's parents.

54
00:02:51.727 --> 00:02:53.748
"Come on, you guys," Maggie said to the others.

55
00:02:57.356 --> 00:02:58.176
"We have one more treasure to find!"

56
00:02:58.196 --> 00:02:58.957
They all ran to the bandstand.

57
00:02:58.977 --> 00:02:59.917
A cooler with a skull and crossbones sat there.

58
00:02:59.937 --> 00:03:00.778
Henry read the note that was taped to it.

59
00:03:00.798 --> 00:03:02.639
"We're supposed to carry the cooler back to William's beach house," he informed his friends.

60
00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:03.559
"It will get filled up with something there."

61
00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:07.642
As they hurried back to William's house, The Lemonade Detectives talked about the case.

62
00:03:07.662 --> 00:03:09.222
"How did you figure out that Anna was the thief?"

63
00:03:09.262 --> 00:03:09.743
Maggie asked Henry.

64
00:03:09.763 --> 00:03:10.363
Henry shrugged.

65
00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:12.484
"It was the only answer that fit all the clues."

66
00:03:12.504 --> 00:03:16.646
"A few things still don't make sense though," Cole said.

67
00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:19.488
"Why was Nathan acting weird all day?"

68
00:03:20.529 --> 00:03:21.529
They looked at Nathan.

69
00:03:21.549 --> 00:03:24.671
"Ah-choo!" Nathan sneezed.

70
00:03:25.511 --> 00:03:26.392
Henry smiled.

71
00:03:27.548 --> 00:03:29.570
"Another case closed," he said.

72
00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:33.132
"Nathan caught his sister's cold and isn't feeling well.

73
00:03:33.492 --> 00:03:35.153
That's why he's grumpy today!"

74
00:03:35.173 --> 00:03:38.035
"Okay," Maggie said.

75
00:03:38.055 --> 00:03:40.257
"But I have another question.

76
00:03:41.158 --> 00:03:43.619
Why was Roger hanging around us all day?"

77
00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.561
They'd just come within view of the beach house.

78
00:03:47.522 --> 00:03:48.263
Henry pointed.

79
00:03:48.283 --> 00:03:51.645
"I think we just solved that mystery too."

80
00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:55.508
There was a party set up on the deck with pirate decorations!

81
00:03:56.872 --> 00:03:59.193
Roger stood there, dressed in a pirate costume.

82
00:03:59.914 --> 00:04:01.195
"Ahoy, mateys!"

83
00:04:01.515 --> 00:04:02.595
he called, waving.

84
00:04:02.615 --> 00:04:08.719
"Come and enjoy your final booty—it's a pirate party!"

85
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:15.123
They brought the cooler over, and Roger immediately filled it with ice and soda for them.

86
00:04:16.424 --> 00:04:21.026
Henry could see Anna standing off to the side, talking with William's parents in low tones.

87
00:04:22.287 --> 00:04:23.828
Henry and Maggie were watching her.

88
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.301
"Do you think Anna and William can still be friends?"

89
00:04:27.662 --> 00:04:28.842
asked Maggie softly.

90
00:04:28.862 --> 00:04:31.984
"I'm not sure," Henry replied.

91
00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:38.308
"Anna seems pretty sorry about what she did, but friends don't steal from friends."

92
00:04:38.328 --> 00:04:45.491
"And cousins don't steal from cousins," Maggie added, banging her cup gently against Henry's.

93
00:04:45.511 --> 00:04:50.554
"Your parents must have set up this party while we were in town," Cole said to William.

94
00:04:51.635 --> 00:04:53.436
William grinned as he looked around the deck.

95
00:04:54.292 --> 00:04:55.653
"It's pretty cool, actually."

96
00:04:55.673 --> 00:05:00.257
"That's why Roger went to the general store earlier," Henry chimed in.

97
00:05:00.277 --> 00:05:03.920
"Anna's parents also do catering, remember?

98
00:05:04.681 --> 00:05:06.442
Roger must have been picking up the food."

99
00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:08.364
Maggie laughed.

100
00:05:08.384 --> 00:05:13.148
"It's a good thing we solved all the mysteries," she said.

101
00:05:13.168 --> 00:05:18.972
"Otherwise—" Just then Roger Redbeard popped up from behind Maggie.

102
00:05:18.992 --> 00:05:21.875
"I would have made you walk the plank!"

103
00:05:22.335 --> 00:05:22.956
he finished.
